// The images the headline runtime metric is the geometric mean over, equal weight each, built by
// build.sh. Every expectation is pinned: retired is the instruction count at the breakpoint that
// ends the run, and checksum is the CRC-32 of the console buffer left in the C return register
// there, so an alternative that decodes or executes anything differently cannot reproduce it by
// accident. The programs both architectures share agree on the checksum across two instruction
// sets and two semantic implementations.
